3531   E3E4             ;This is unused in the macros. You must call it directly at $F1D5
3532   E3E4             ;The behavior of this command is probably the most complex. It 
3533   E3E4             ;starts at the last lamp in the range. If it is already set, then
3534   E3E4             ;the routine simply exits. If the last lamp is not set, the routine
3535   E3E4             ;goes down through each lamp in the range. If if finds a lamp on,
3536   E3E4             ;then it turns off that lamp, then goes back up to the next lamp
3537   E3E4             ;and turns it on. If no lamps are on in the range, then the first
3538   E3E4             ;lamp in the range is turned on.
3539   E3E4             ;The best example of this routine is for the 10-20-30 lamps on 
3540   E3E4             ;Jungle Lord. It will simply incrment the 10-20-30 lamps sequentially
3541   E3E4             ;and then stop at 30. If none are on, then it will turn on 10.
3542   E3E4             lampm_g             
