5742   F08F             ;**********************************************************************************
5743   F08F             ;* NMI Routines - This section of code is run only when the 
5744   F08F             ;*                diagnostic switch on the CPU board is pressed.
5745   F08F             ;*                It will test the hardware and report any errors
5746   F08F             ;*                via the LED display on the CPU board. If all tests
5747   F08F             ;*                are passed, the LED display will show '0' and
5748   F08F             ;*                the code jumps to the normal power-up routines.
5749   F08F             ;*
5750   F08F             ;* Errors are as Follows:
5751   F08F             ;*
5752   F08F             ;*      0 - Test Passed
5753   F08F             ;*      1 - IC13 RAM Fault (Most Significant Nybble)
5754   F08F             ;*      2 - IC16 RAM Fault (Least Significant Nybble)
5755   F08F             ;*      3 - IC17 ROM 2 Fault (Location $F000-$FFFF)
5756   F08F             ;*      4 - IC14 ROM 1 Fault (Location $E000-$EFFF)
5757   F08F             ;*      5 - IC20 ROM 0 Fault (Location $D000-$DFFF)
5758   F08F             ;*      6 - Not Used
5759   F08F             ;*      7 - Not Used
5760   F08F             ;*      8 - IC19 CMOS RAM Fault or Memory Protect Failure
5761   F08F             ;*      9 - Coin Door Closed or Memory Protect Failure or IC19 CMOS RAM Fault
5762   F08F             ;**********************************************************************************
